      "content": "High-dose Vitamin C is not a proven or safe antibiotic replacement for a UTI, especially when you have existing kidney issues. Excessive vitamin intake, particularly with compromised kidneys, can sometimes lead to problems. For immediate discomfort, over-the-counter pain relievers are sometimes used as temporary relief, but you still need a proper diagnosis for treatment. Please try to reach a telehealth service or nurse line if an in-person visit isn't possible today.",
